 "vlm_pair_verdict": "1. **Sharper:** Image 1 (the Marble kitchen) is clearly sharper — cabinet frames, mullions, tile grout lines and countertop edges are all well defined.\n\n2. **Blurry/veiled/dotted:** Image 2 (moradi_main1) — everything is heavily blurred/veiled; there's also a faint dot/grid pattern visible on the wall and bedding, indicating sparse or undersized gaussians.\n\n3. **Black holes / missing content:** Image 1 actually shows some dark voids inside the glazed cabinets (plates float over black), whereas Image 2 has no hard black holes — its problem is blur, not missing geometry.\n\n4. **Artifacts:**\n   - Image 1: mild smearing/streaking in the plates behind glass, slight waviness in tile lines; no floaters or banding.\n   - Image 2: strong overall smearing/blur, a regular dot/grid texture artifact across flat surfaces, soft \"melting\" edges (e.g., picture frame, bed legs); no obvious black-hole floaters.\n\n5. **Verdict:** Since both images use the same engine/camera, the gap is mainly in **content quality/density** of the splat reconstruction (sparse, low-resolution gaussians in moradi_main1), not in the renderer itself."
}